SCAMAI — AI-DRIVEN SPAM DETECTION & SCAM-ENGAGEMENT SYSTEM — PROPRIETARY LICENCE

Copyright (c) 2026 The ScamAI Project Team — MSc "Cybersecurity and Artificial
Intelligence Technologies", University of Piraeus. All rights reserved.

This repository contains the complete source code of an academic group project
(an MSc assignment for the University of Piraeus): a two-stage system for
detecting scam/spam email and engaging with scammers. The first stage is a
Random Forest classifier (with a Multinomial Naive Bayes baseline) trained on a
consolidated dataset of 13,919 emails drawn from three sources — a synthetic
template set, the Enron Fraud corpus and the SpamAssassin corpus — using eight
interpretable, hand-crafted features. The second stage is a generative-AI
"scambaiting" responder that detects the scam type, adopts a matching persona
and drafts time-wasting replies, protected by an output safety layer (redaction
of PII, IBANs, cards and crypto wallets; blocking of physical meetings,
addresses, threats and abuse) and by prompt-injection defences that treat the
incoming email as untrusted data, with multi-turn support and pluggable
providers (an offline mock provider plus Anthropic Claude, OpenAI and Google
Gemini). The repository also includes the preprocessing pipeline, the trained
model artefact, unit tests, a Streamlit demonstration UI, and the accompanying
report, presentation and documentation.

Publishing this repository does not place any of it in the public domain and
does not grant any licence beyond what is stated below.


