────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ACADEMIC INTEGRITY AND RESPONSIBLE USE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This project was produced as an educational exercise. It is shared for study,
review and demonstration purposes only.

It must not be submitted, in whole or in part, as anyone else's academic work.
Whoever uses this repository is solely responsible for complying with the
academic-integrity rules of their own institution. The authors accept no
responsibility for any consequences of plagiarism or misuse.

This project studies scam detection and automated scam engagement for
defensive, educational purposes. The system is fully SIMULATED: it never sends
email, never contacts any real person, and produces only draft replies intended
for human review and approval (human-in-the-loop). The scambaiting responder
must not be used to engage, deceive, harass, provoke or retaliate against any
person, to conduct any campaign against real individuals, organisations or
systems, or in any way that could lead to real-world contact or escalation.

The scam emails included are synthetic or drawn from public research corpora and
target no real individual. The detection and response logic here is a laboratory
prototype evaluated on small, curated datasets; it is not hardened, audited or
intended for production use, and must not be relied upon to protect, or to act
on behalf of, any real system or real user without independent review.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONFIGURATION AND DATA
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

No real API keys, service credentials or other secrets are contained in this
repository. The provided .env.example is a template only; any real keys are
supplied locally by the user and are never committed.

All email addresses, names, domain names and monetary figures appearing in the
synthetic dataset are fabricated laboratory examples. The real-world corpora
(Enron, SpamAssassin) are public datasets used for research; they are not
redistributed here and must be obtained from their original sources under their
own terms. The results, logs and model artefacts contain no personal data about
any of the authors or any third party. Any resemblance to real identifiers is
coincidental.


